Subject: vg rna: release augment translations and drain edited paths inside augment_graph

Stage A opportunity 2. Applies on top of 0001. Frees the vector<Translation>
(two protobuf Translations per graph node) as soon as translation_index has
been built instead of at function return, frees the exon boundary Paths once
augment() has consumed them, and erases each edited transcript path as soon as
its CompletedTranscriptPath exists so the two representations cross over
instead of stacking. augment_graph now takes the edited list by non-const
reference; both callers own a local list they never read again. See README.md.

